  ('d326a9f3-f650-47ac-ae52-f85f8d5cb361', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_063', 'P2', 'P2_part_a', 'define', 2, 'AO1', NULL, 'Define the term "positive externality of production."', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T17:18:03.919+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V3', 'pass'),
  ('45b12293-fdb3-4e0e-ac86-4c950c241bb8', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_065', 'P2', 'P2_part_a', 'calculate', 2, 'AO4', NULL, 'Calculate the total external cost imposed on society when 120 tonnes of fish are harvested from the shared lake per month.', 'A shared lake is used by multiple fishing villages. The private cost of harvesting fish is $40 per tonne, while the social cost is $55 per tonne. Each month, fishing boats collectively harvest 120 tonnes of fish.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T17:18:17.486+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('029f655f-50aa-48aa-b189-8e67abec6064', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_069', 'P2', 'P2_part_a', 'define', 2, 'AO1', NULL, 'Define the term "carbon tax."', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T17:18:28.51+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V3', 'pass'),
  ('bb967b92-10fd-4357-a85f-e64249e5dc60', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_096', 'P2', 'P2_part_a', 'calculate', 2, 'AO4', NULL, 'Calculate the Gross National Income (GNI) per capita of Valdoria.', 'Valdoria has a Gross Domestic Product (GDP) of $480 billion. Its citizens earn $18 billion in net factor income from abroad, and Valdoria has a population of 60 million.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T17:20:59.63+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('a34c234d-f488-4f48-ab04-6f5ef9992fc7', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_090', 'P2', 'P2_part_b', 'explain', 3, 'AO2', NULL, 'Explain why a rise in household saving can lead to a fall in national income.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T17:19:40.406+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V3', 'pass'),
  ('2c096ebf-60f3-41b6-9545-556f6b319731', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_091', 'P2', 'P2_part_b', 'explain', 3, 'AO2', NULL, 'Explain how the expenditure approach is used to calculate nominal GDP.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T17:19:51.224+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V3', 'pass'),
  ('f498e0e9-7ad8-4c53-9102-f32d83ca79ad', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_092', 'P2', 'P2_part_b', 'explain', 3, 'AO2', NULL, 'Explain why a country''s nominal Gross National Income (GNI) may differ from its nominal Gross Domestic Product (GDP).', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T17:20:04.519+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V3', 'pass'),
  ('e79ea267-7ccf-4429-88a7-b061d654b596', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_094', 'P2', 'P2_part_b', 'calculate', 3, 'AO4', NULL, 'Calculate the GDP per capita (PPP) for Valdoria, expressing your answer in international dollars.', 'Valdoria has a nominal GDP of 900 billion Valdorian pesos and a population of 45 million. The PPP conversion factor is 3 Valdorian pesos per international dollar.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T17:20:42.688+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V3', 'pass'),
  ('b390d030-d831-4849-9816-c4f15cbf4e7d', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_110', 'P2', 'P2_part_b', 'calculate', 3, 'AO4', NULL, 'Calculate the unemployment rate and the labour force participation rate for Country X using the data provided.', 'Country X has a working-age population of 40 million people. Of these, 24 million are employed, 6 million are actively seeking work but unable to find it, and the remaining 10 million are neither employed nor actively seeking work.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T17:11:08.021+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V3', 'borderline'),
  ('03749dd6-7647-4fb0-aa38-0205a31ca58c', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_113', 'P2', 'P2_part_b', 'explain', 3, 'AO2', NULL, 'Explain one reason why the Consumer Price Index (CPI) may overstate the true rate of inflation experienced by households.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T17:28:59.603+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V3', 'pass'),
  ('74ea640e-3f4b-495a-8f47-20906914a103', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_124', 'P2', 'P2_part_b', 'calculate', 3, 'AO4', NULL, 'Calculate the percentage of the population living in absolute poverty in Country X.', 'In Country X, the international absolute poverty line is set at $2.15 per person per day. A recent household survey found that out of a total population of 4,000,000 people, 680,000 individuals have a daily income below this threshold.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T18:31:03.521+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V3', 'pass'),
  ('410332d9-e52d-4ead-abaf-f61832201e06', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_093', 'P2', 'P2_part_c_f', 'explain', 4, 'AO2', NULL, 'Explain why a rise in nominal GDP may overstate the improvement in a country''s standard of living when inflation is rising.', 'Nordavia''s nominal GDP grew by 8% in 2023, while its GDP deflator rose from 100 to 106 over the same period. Policymakers are debating whether this growth represents a genuine increase in the nation''s output and welfare.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T17:20:29.232+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('ccb5e2c1-b268-495c-bf64-f189af4ebc24', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_098', 'P2', 'P2_part_c_f', 'explain', 4, 'AO2', NULL, 'Explain how a rise in consumer confidence is likely to affect the aggregate demand (AD) curve in Verantia.', 'Verantia is a small open economy that has recently experienced a period of falling unemployment and rising household incomes. Surveys indicate that consumers are increasingly optimistic about their future financial prospects.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T17:21:39.878+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('f96d3c29-dad6-47af-90cf-aca39a7b087e', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_099', 'P2', 'P2_part_c_f', 'distinguish', 4, 'AO2', NULL, 'Distinguish between the marginal propensity to consume (MPC) and the marginal propensity to save (MPS) as determinants of household consumption decisions.', 'Following a period of rising real incomes, households in Verdania increased their total spending on goods and services from $420 billion to $460 billion, while aggregate saving rose from $80 billion to $100 billion. Economists are examining how income changes are allocated between consumption and saving.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T17:21:53.789+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('41d684ec-5678-47a4-a35d-20be2d93b83f', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_105', 'P2', 'P2_part_c_f', 'distinguish', 4, 'AO2', NULL, 'Distinguish between an inflationary gap and a deflationary (recessionary) gap in an economy.', 'Ravonia, a mid-sized open economy, has experienced fluctuating levels of aggregate demand over the past decade, resulting in periods where real GDP has deviated significantly from its potential output of $500 billion — sometimes exceeding it, and at other times falling well short.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T17:24:02.155+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('d8d3bdcc-6d21-49f8-b1ec-8451b3c3c89b', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_108', 'P2', 'P2_part_c_f', 'explain', 4, 'AO2', NULL, 'Explain how an increase in government spending on infrastructure can lead to actual economic growth in an economy operating below full employment.', 'Meridonia, a developing economy, is currently operating with significant unemployment and underutilised productive capacity. The government has announced a $12 billion infrastructure investment programme, funding new roads, bridges, and digital networks across the country.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T17:24:31.51+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('5eb6383e-fbda-4e4a-a979-b2a3867dcde2', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_112', 'P2', 'P2_part_c_f', 'explain', 4, 'AO2', NULL, 'Explain two costs of unemployment for the government of Nordavia.', 'Nordavia, a mid-sized economy, has seen its unemployment rate rise from 4.2% to 9.7% over the past two years following a sharp contraction in its manufacturing sector. The government is facing growing pressure on its public finances as the number of jobless workers continues to increase.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T17:28:49.289+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('24c78813-53f4-4190-903e-e1701b783f3c', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_114', 'P2', 'P2_part_c_f', 'distinguish', 4, 'AO2', NULL, 'Distinguish between demand-pull inflation and cost-push inflation as possible explanations for the rising price level in Valdoria.', 'Valdoria, a mid-sized open economy, has recently recorded a sustained rise in its general price level. Economists are debating whether the inflation stems from strong consumer spending fuelled by tax cuts or from soaring global energy and raw material prices driving up firms'' production costs.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T17:29:23.433+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('7fc7400d-1899-459c-8d3c-90d1e948ab65', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_121', 'P2', 'P2_part_c_f', 'explain', 4, 'AO2', NULL, 'Explain why a country with a Gini coefficient of 0.55 experiences greater economic inequality than one with a Gini coefficient of 0.30.', 'Country A and Country B have similar levels of GDP per capita, yet their income distributions differ markedly: Country A records a Gini coefficient of 0.55, while Country B records a Gini coefficient of 0.30.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T17:31:22.901+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('dd123ffa-ec4c-4498-971b-370c65c5df84', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_128', 'P2', 'P2_part_c_f', 'explain', 4, 'AO2', NULL, 'Explain how a progressive income tax system can reduce income inequality in an economy.', 'The government of Valdoria has recently reformed its income tax structure, replacing a flat 20% tax rate with a tiered system in which earners in the lowest bracket pay 10%, middle-income earners pay 25%, and the highest earners pay 45%. Transfer payments funded by tax revenue are distributed to low-income households.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T18:31:27.967+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('69b3a9b9-6063-47ef-b222-27a581af9498', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_131', 'P2', 'P2_part_c_f', 'explain', 4, 'AO2', NULL, 'Explain how an increase in the central bank''s benchmark interest rate can reduce inflationary pressure in an economy.', 'The central bank of Arvonia has observed a sharp rise in the annual inflation rate, climbing from 2% to 7% over six months. In response, the central bank has announced an increase in the benchmark interest rate from 1.5% to 4.0%.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T18:31:40.007+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('45012b70-6296-43f9-bc71-485f536364f2', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_147', 'P2', 'P2_part_c_f', 'distinguish', 4, 'AO2', NULL, 'Distinguish between an expansionary fiscal policy and a contractionary fiscal policy in the context of managing an economy''s output gap.', 'The government of Valdoria is facing a significant negative output gap following a sharp decline in consumer spending and business investment. Policymakers are debating whether fiscal intervention is appropriate and, if so, what form it should take.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T18:32:04.463+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('c1c1599f-517d-40a0-bf04-80bf06ce78c4', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_148', 'P2', 'P2_part_c_f', 'explain', 4, 'AO2', NULL, 'Explain how supply-side policies can help a government achieve long-run economic growth.', 'The government of Valdoria, a developing economy, has announced a package of supply-side policies aimed at raising the productive capacity of the economy. These measures include increased funding for worker training programmes and substantial tax incentives for private investment in new capital equipment.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T18:32:18.218+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('42950d96-f1a5-4b09-a29d-7bb234ee5cef', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_151', 'P2', 'P2_part_c_f', 'distinguish', 4, 'AO2', NULL, 'Distinguish between supply-side fiscal policies that directly lower production costs for firms and those that aim to increase the productive capacity of an economy through investment in human capital.', 'The government of Valdoria has announced a dual-pronged fiscal package: a 5 percentage point cut in corporate tax rates alongside a $2 billion increase in annual spending on vocational training programmes. Economists debate which of the two measures will deliver more sustained long-run economic growth.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T18:33:01.125+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('ad19e835-3bdd-4203-8e55-b18048d29896', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_161', 'P2', 'P2_part_c_f', 'analyse', 4, 'AO2', NULL, 'Analyse the likely effects of an export subsidy granted by a government to its domestic wheat producers on the volume of wheat traded in the international market.', 'The government of Arvonia, a major wheat-producing nation, introduces an export subsidy of $40 per tonne to boost its agricultural sector''s competitiveness abroad. Prior to the subsidy, Arvonian wheat exporters held a 12% share of the global wheat market.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T18:34:22.829+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('622421dd-fa71-45da-8695-2953b10fc07b', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_165', 'P2', 'P2_part_c_f', 'distinguish', 4, 'AO2', NULL, 'Distinguish between a tariff and an import quota as methods of trade protection.', 'Ardovia, a small open economy, has recently faced pressure from domestic manufacturers to shield local industries from cheaper foreign competition. The government is debating whether to impose trade protection measures, with critics arguing that such policies ultimately reduce economic efficiency and consumer welfare.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T19:56:29.089+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V3', 'pass'),
  ('c60f6eb1-a112-481b-b83c-70aec2a33c65', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_168', 'P2', 'P2_part_c_f', 'calculate', 4, 'AO4', NULL, 'Calculate the trade creation effect (in USD billion) for Country A following its entry into a free trade area, and the percentage change in consumer surplus as a result of the price change.', 'Before joining the free trade area, Country A imposed a tariff of $20 per unit on imported steel, raising the domestic price to $120 per unit; at this price, domestic consumption was 80 million units and domestic production was 50 million units. After joining the free trade area, the tariff on imports from member countries is eliminated, lowering the price to $100 per unit, at which domestic consumption rises to 100 million units and domestic production falls to 35 million units. Consumer surplus before joining the free trade area was $240 billion.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T19:57:31.148+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('2232f0da-c953-4ae2-8d7b-4dbfab255576', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_173', 'P2', 'P2_part_c_f', 'analyse', 4, 'AO2', NULL, 'Analyse how the WTO''s dispute settlement mechanism may help reduce trade conflicts between member countries.', 'In 2023, two WTO member countries became embroiled in a trade dispute after one imposed tariffs of 35% on the other''s steel exports, alleging unfair subsidisation. The affected country filed a formal complaint with the WTO, triggering its dispute settlement process.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T19:57:45.505+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('f41c2032-e847-4100-a845-0a18839d7fa3', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_177', 'P2', 'P2_part_c_f', 'analyse', 4, 'AO2', NULL, 'Analyse how a central bank may maintain a fixed exchange rate when persistent capital outflows place downward pressure on the currency.', 'Argentia, a small open economy, operates under a fixed exchange rate regime, pegging its currency (the argent) to the US dollar at AR 5 = USD 1. In recent months, falling commodity export revenues and rising interest rates abroad have triggered sustained capital outflows, causing the argent to weaken toward the lower bound of its permitted band.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T19:58:47.477+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('ea9b44ad-4653-4d9f-bf0e-bd9e18491057', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_191', 'P2', 'P2_part_c_f', 'calculate', 4, 'AO4', NULL, 'Calculate the adult literacy rate for Country Malvernia, showing all your working.', 'Country Malvernia has a total population of 40 million, of which 25 million are aged 15 and above. Of those aged 15 and above, 18 million are able to read and write.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T19:59:40.402+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('cc49afd3-b64d-4764-ba8b-e9a79f9c2d59', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_195', 'P2', 'P2_part_c_f', 'analyse', 4, 'AO2', NULL, 'Analyse how low levels of education can trap households in a cycle of poverty.', 'In the rural regions of Malawi, approximately 70% of households earn less than $2.15 per day, leaving families unable to afford school fees, nutritious food, or basic healthcare. Survey data shows that children from the poorest households are three times less likely to complete secondary education than those from higher-income families.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T20:00:10.686+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('b1bf3735-13a5-4f83-b868-8403b09ff8c3', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_196', 'P2', 'P2_part_c_f', 'calculate', 4, 'AO4', NULL, 'Calculate the percentage change in GDP per capita between 2023 and 2024 for Maloria. (Show all working.)', 'In 2023, Maloria — a low-income country heavily dependent on agricultural exports — had a nominal GDP of $48 billion and a population of 32 million. By 2024, nominal GDP had risen to $52.8 billion while the population grew to 33.6 million.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T20:00:28.308+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('92a1b153-6092-4d91-8d78-ec2db5744635', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_201', 'P2', 'P2_part_c_f', 'calculate', 4, 'AO4', NULL, 'Calculate the profit or loss made by each of GreenLoop''s two divisions in the most recent financial year, and calculate the overall profit or loss for the enterprise as a whole. [4]', 'GreenLoop, a social enterprise operating in the recycling sector, generates revenue from two divisions: its core recycling operations and a newly diversified urban farming unit. In its most recent financial year, GreenLoop''s total revenue was $480,000, with the urban farming unit accounting for 35% of total revenue. The recycling division reported total costs of $195,000, and the urban farming unit reported total costs of $112,000.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T20:01:51.998+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('fafab801-f442-418c-a289-4ddd4ee52c24', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_166', 'P2', 'P2_part_g', 'evaluate', 15, 'AO3', NULL, 'Evaluate the view that the government of Valdoria should abandon its current protectionist policies and fully embrace free trade.', 'Valdoria is a lower-middle-income economy with a GDP of $42 billion and an annual GDP growth rate of 2.1%. The government currently imposes a 35% tariff on imported manufactured goods to shield its domestic industries, which employ approximately 18% of the labour force, amid an unemployment rate of 9.4%. Despite these protectionist measures, Valdoria''s current account deficit has widened to 6.8% of GDP over the past three years, and the World Bank estimates that removing trade barriers could increase Valdoria''s real GDP by up to 4.5% over a decade through efficiency gains and greater export market access.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T19:56:46.519+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('57c96910-634a-4018-a248-f1edbc9980bd', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_175', 'P2', 'P2_part_g', 'evaluate', 15, 'AO3', NULL, 'Evaluate the likely effects of a rising interest rate differential and a deteriorating current account balance on the exchange rate of the peso.', 'Cordelia is a small, open economy that operates under a floating exchange rate regime. In 2023, the Central Bank of Cordelia raised its benchmark interest rate from 4.5% to 8.0% in response to annual inflation reaching 11.2%, while its major trading partners maintained rates near 3.0%. Despite this monetary tightening, Cordelia''s current account deficit widened from 3.1% to 6.4% of GDP over the same period, driven by surging import demand as real GDP growth remained robust at 5.8%. The Cordelian peso had already appreciated by 12% against a trade-weighted basket of currencies in the first half of 2023 before markets began reassessing its outlook in Q3.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T19:58:14.066+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V3', 'pass'),
  ('7d0c9387-6a06-42ed-937b-bf5c648b714b', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_176', 'P2', 'P2_part_g', 'discuss', 15, 'AO3', NULL, 'Discuss the consequences of the depreciation of the korona on Nordavia''s macroeconomic performance.', 'Nordavia is a small, open economy in which exports and imports together account for approximately 74% of GDP. Between 2021 and 2023, the Nordavian korona depreciated by 22% against its major trading partners'' currencies, largely due to a persistent current account deficit and falling foreign direct investment inflows. Over the same period, the annual inflation rate rose from 2.1% to 6.8%, while the unemployment rate fell modestly from 7.4% to 6.9%, and real GDP growth edged up from 1.2% to 2.5%.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T19:58:29.996+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('3e43f1e2-f05e-469e-aee7-68f3e8f3c752', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_194', 'P2', 'P2_part_g', 'discuss', 15, 'AO3', NULL, 'Discuss the view that economic growth always leads to improved economic development in Valdoria.', 'Valdoria, a lower-middle-income country in Southeast Asia, has recorded an average annual real GDP growth rate of 6.2% over the past decade, driven largely by exports of raw materials and a booming manufacturing sector. Despite this growth, the country''s Human Development Index (HDI) score has risen only marginally from 0.54 to 0.57 over the same period, and the Gini coefficient currently stands at 0.48, indicating high income inequality. Unemployment remains at 11.3%, with significant underemployment in rural areas, while access to secondary education stands at just 54% and approximately 19% of the population lacks access to clean drinking water. The government has prioritised attracting foreign direct investment (FDI) through low corporate tax rates, resulting in limited public revenue available for social spending.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T19:59:56.492+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('69ece6d3-5bc7-4778-ad73-0fd7c3866813', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_197', 'P2', 'P2_part_g', 'examine', 15, 'AO3', NULL, 'Examine the view that a combination of a large informal economy and high levels of external debt represents the most significant barrier to sustainable economic development in countries such as Mavalika.', 'Mavalika is a landlocked low-income country in sub-Saharan Africa with a GDP per capita of approximately $820 (current USD). An estimated 74% of its labour force operates within the informal economy, limiting the government''s tax revenue to just 11% of GDP. External debt stands at 92% of GDP, with annual debt-servicing costs consuming 28% of government expenditure, while net capital outflows averaged $340 million per year between 2018 and 2023. Mavalika''s official unemployment rate is recorded at 8.4%, though underemployment within the informal sector is widely believed to be substantially higher.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T20:01:01.929+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V3', 'pass'),
  ('1035c978-0746-49ee-9994-f48999a77aea', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_200', 'P2', 'P2_part_g', 'discuss', 15, 'AO3', NULL, 'Discuss the view that export-led growth is a more effective trade strategy for economic development than import substitution industrialisation (ISI).', 'Ravoria is a lower-middle-income country with a GDP per capita of $2,340 and an average annual GDP growth rate of 2.1% over the past decade. Unemployment stands at 18.4%, and the country runs a persistent current account deficit equivalent to 6.2% of GDP. The government is debating whether to continue its existing ISI policy — which has raised manufacturing''s share of GDP from 9% to 14% over 15 years but relies on tariffs averaging 32% — or to pivot toward an export-led growth strategy by joining a regional free trade agreement and depreciating its currency by an estimated 15%.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T20:01:19.317+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('c36e34f0-d5b3-4caa-b1b0-5b0dbddf98fa', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_206', 'P2', 'P2_part_g', 'evaluate', 15, 'AO3', NULL, 'Evaluate the effectiveness of World Bank and IMF conditional lending programmes as a means of promoting long-run economic development in low-income countries.', 'Nambara, a low-income country in sub-Saharan Africa, has a GDP per capita of USD 820, an annual inflation rate of 18.4%, and an unemployment rate of 31%. Facing a balance of payments crisis and a fiscal deficit equivalent to 9.2% of GDP, the government approached the IMF for a USD 1.4 billion Extended Credit Facility loan and the World Bank for USD 600 million in structural adjustment financing. Both institutions attached conditions requiring Nambara to reduce public spending by 12%, liberalise trade by cutting average tariffs from 22% to 8%, and privatise three state-owned enterprises within 24 months.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T20:02:21.159+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V3', 'pass'),
  ('aec60567-860a-413a-a15a-0f9a44956587', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'SL', 'IB_ECON_209', 'P2', 'P2_part_g', 'examine', 15, 'AO3', NULL, 'Examine the view that market-oriented approaches are more effective than interventionist approaches in promoting economic development in countries such as Marvelia.', 'Marvelia is a lower-middle-income country with a GDP per capita of USD 2,340 and an annual GDP growth rate of 2.1%. Unemployment stands at 18.4%, with youth unemployment reaching 31%, and inflation has averaged 9.7% over the past five years. In 2018, Marvelia adopted a structural adjustment programme recommended by the IMF, which included privatisation of state-owned enterprises, tariff reductions from 28% to 6%, and cuts to public spending on education and healthcare; by 2023, foreign direct investment inflows rose from USD 180 million to USD 540 million, yet the national poverty rate remained at 43% and the Gini coefficient worsened from 0.41 to 0.47.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T20:02:49.056+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('97a634a6-5877-4c0e-b46b-ae344ad28988', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'HL', 'IB_ECON_007', 'P3', 'P3_part_a', 'calculate', 4, 'AO4', NULL, 'Calculate the equilibrium level of national income for the economy described in the context, and calculate the value of the multiplier.', 'In a hypothetical economy, autonomous consumption is $200 billion, investment is $150 billion, government spending is $250 billion, and exports are $180 billion. The marginal propensity to consume (MPC) is 0.6, the marginal rate of taxation (MRT) is 0.2, and the marginal propensity to import (MPM) is 0.1.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T15:56:30.201+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('9a31ba0a-c9a4-48e5-99b4-b15eae5d0bfe', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'HL', 'IB_ECON_009', 'P3', 'P3_part_a', 'calculate', 4, 'AO4', NULL, 'Calculate the percentage change in quantity demanded of Good X and the price elasticity of demand (PED) for Good X, using the data in the context. Show all working.', 'An economist is testing a demand model for Good X, holding all other variables constant (ceteris paribus). When the price of Good X rises from $20 to $25, the quantity demanded falls from 800 units to 680 units per week.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T15:56:58.278+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('10b2741b-1a84-4a0f-a07b-eda457acaab8', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'HL', 'IB_ECON_018', 'P3', 'P3_part_a', 'calculate', 4, 'AO4', NULL, 'Calculate the price elasticity of demand (PED) for electric scooters using the data in the table below, and state whether demand is elastic or inelastic at this price range.
