  ('094f3a9d-3ec5-4159-985b-f027fad9eaa5', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'HL', 'IB_ECON_093', 'P3', 'P3_part_b', 'recommend', 10, 'AO3', NULL, 'Recommend whether the government of Veralonia should use real GDP or real GNI as its primary macroeconomic indicator when designing its poverty-reduction spending programme.', 'Veralonia is a lower-middle-income economy with a large migrant workforce abroad; in 2023, remittance inflows accounted for 18% of national income, while net factor income from abroad was +$14.2 billion. Official data show that Veralonia''s real GDP growth rate was 3.1% in 2023, whereas its real GNI growth rate was 5.6% over the same period, reflecting the significant contribution of overseas workers to household incomes.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T17:20:18.214+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('902dff3e-49ad-4907-b4c6-eadfe353efbd', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'HL', 'IB_ECON_097', 'P3', 'P3_part_b', 'recommend', 10, 'AO3', NULL, 'Recommend whether Bhutan''s government should replace its Gross National Happiness (GNH) index with the United Nations Human Development Index (HDI) as its primary measure of national well-being.', 'Bhutan has long used Gross National Happiness (GNH) as its primary measure of societal progress, yet recent data reveal a growing divergence between GNH scores and material living standards: GDP per capita stands at approximately USD 3,300, while 28% of the rural population lacks reliable access to clean drinking water and the youth unemployment rate has risen to 22%. The government is under pressure to adopt an alternative or supplementary well-being framework to better guide resource allocation and international development partnerships.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T17:21:26.209+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('190ede03-25b4-4478-8b0d-cc17eaf24e0c', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'HL', 'IB_ECON_099', 'P3', 'P3_part_b', 'recommend', 10, 'AO3', NULL, 'Recommend one policy measure the Brazilian government should adopt to restore private investment growth.', 'Brazil''s gross fixed capital formation fell from 19.2% of GDP in 2019 to 16.8% in 2023, reflecting a prolonged contraction in private investment. The central bank''s benchmark Selic interest rate averaged 12.75% over 2023, while business confidence indices remained well below their 2017 peak. Simultaneously, household consumption growth slowed to 1.4% in real terms, in part because rising debt-service burdens constrained disposable income.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T17:22:08.689+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('d4de721e-a7c3-4967-9337-15afd5f1bbb6', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'HL', 'IB_ECON_105', 'P3', 'P3_part_b', 'recommend', 10, 'AO3', NULL, 'Recommend a macroeconomic policy response that the Turkish government should adopt to address the current inflationary gap in its economy.', 'Turkey''s economy is operating significantly above its potential output, with the annual inflation rate reaching 68% in 2024 and real GDP growth running at 4.5% — well above the long-run trend rate of approximately 2.5%. The central bank''s benchmark interest rate stands at 45%, yet aggregate demand pressures, fuelled by strong consumer spending and a fiscal deficit equivalent to 5.2% of GDP, continue to push the price level upward.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T17:24:17.26+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('f2328909-a229-4a5c-87fd-9004f01da01c', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'HL', 'IB_ECON_124', 'P3', 'P3_part_b', 'recommend', 10, 'AO3', NULL, 'Recommend whether the government of Malawi should adopt an absolute poverty line or a relative poverty measure as its primary benchmark for designing and targeting its national social protection programmes.', 'Malawi is one of the lowest-income countries in sub-Saharan Africa, with approximately 70% of its population living below the World Bank''s international absolute poverty line of $2.15 per day (2022 PPP). Despite this, rising income inequality — reflected in a Gini coefficient of 0.45 — means that a significant share of households above the absolute poverty threshold still cannot afford basic social participation relative to the median standard of living.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T17:31:42.943+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('811b3dbb-c539-4c08-8a1e-5dcbfee42077', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'HL', 'IB_ECON_127', 'P3', 'P3_part_b', 'recommend', 10, 'AO3', NULL, 'Recommend one macroeconomic policy that the Brazilian government should prioritise to reduce income inequality and support long-run economic growth.', 'Brazil has one of the highest levels of income inequality in the world, with a Gini coefficient of 0.53 in 2023, and approximately 33 million people living below the national poverty line. Despite recording GDP growth of 2.9% in 2023, gains have remained concentrated among the top income quintile, with the bottom 20% of households receiving less than 3% of national income.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T18:31:15.752+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('d897409e-c020-4932-8b99-ab887fab3265', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'HL', 'IB_ECON_153', 'P3', 'P3_part_b', 'recommend', 10, 'AO3', NULL, 'Recommend whether the government of Vietnam should remove its existing import tariff on steel products.', 'Vietnam currently imposes a 15% import tariff on foreign steel, which has kept the domestic price of steel at VND 18,500 per kilogram — well above the world price of VND 14,200 per kilogram. Domestic steel producers supply approximately 60% of national demand at the tariff-inclusive price, while the remaining 40% is met by imports. A major national infrastructure expansion programme is forecast to increase total steel demand by 25% over the next three years, raising concerns about supply adequacy and construction cost inflation.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T18:34:09.827+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('62e5da03-a34b-4166-85af-d36b6abb0880', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'HL', 'IB_ECON_161', 'P3', 'P3_part_b', 'recommend', 10, 'AO3', NULL, 'Recommend whether the Indonesian government should remove its existing export subsidy on palm oil producers.', 'Indonesia is the world''s largest palm oil producer, and the government currently provides palm oil exporters with a subsidy equivalent to USD 48 per tonne, costing the national budget approximately USD 2.1 billion annually. Domestic palm oil prices have fallen 22% over the past two years due to oversupply in global markets, squeezing smallholder farmer incomes, while international trading partners have threatened retaliatory tariffs citing unfair trade distortions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T18:34:34.849+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('2c1668d1-8ae4-44d0-b957-409ea17c6ab4', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'HL', 'IB_ECON_167', 'P3', 'P3_part_b', 'recommend', 10, 'AO3', NULL, 'Recommend whether Vietara should pursue membership of a customs union or negotiate a bilateral free trade agreement (FTA) to address its declining export competitiveness.', 'Vietara, a lower-middle-income economy in South-East Asia, has seen its merchandise export growth fall from 8.4% annually in 2018 to just 1.9% in 2023, largely due to high tariff barriers imposed by its three largest trading partners. Vietara currently operates under WTO most-favoured-nation (MFN) rules, with an average applied tariff rate of 12.6% on its key agricultural and manufactured exports. The government is evaluating two preferential trade agreement strategies — joining a regional customs union already encompassing six neighbouring economies, or concluding a bilateral FTA with its single largest trading partner, which accounts for 34% of Vietara''s total export revenue.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T19:57:05.453+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('8ccf1866-d89e-424b-b5a0-49ef9b3f8a5e', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'HL', 'IB_ECON_183', 'P3', 'P3_part_b', 'recommend', 10, 'AO3', NULL, 'Recommend whether the Central Bank of Indonesia should raise domestic interest rates as a policy response to the persistent depreciation of the Indonesian rupiah and the widening deficit on the financial account of its balance of payments.', 'Indonesia''s financial account recorded a net outflow of approximately USD 8.3 billion in 2023, reflecting sustained capital flight as international investors withdrew portfolio investments in search of higher yields abroad. Over the same period, the Indonesian rupiah depreciated by roughly 6% against the US dollar, raising import costs and contributing to inflationary pressure. The Central Bank of Indonesia is now deliberating whether a rise in the benchmark interest rate would be sufficient to reverse capital outflows and stabilise the exchange rate.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T19:59:04.85+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('7f0c8fc5-22c1-49cb-ae7f-bac3380edf48', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'HL', 'IB_ECON_187', 'P3', 'P3_part_b', 'recommend', 10, 'AO3', NULL, 'Recommend one policy response that the South Korean government should adopt to address its persistent current account surplus.', 'South Korea has recorded a current account surplus averaging 4.2% of GDP over the past decade, driven largely by strong export performance in semiconductors and automobiles. Despite this, domestic consumption growth has remained sluggish at 1.8% annually, and trading partners — including the United States and the European Union — have raised concerns about currency undervaluation and imbalanced trade flows. The surplus has contributed to rising foreign reserve accumulation and increased pressure on the Korean won.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T19:59:24.242+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('a131c10e-3aea-4bca-bc21-0d66113859d9', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'HL', 'IB_ECON_197', 'P3', 'P3_part_b', 'recommend', 10, 'AO3', NULL, 'Recommend one policy measure the government of Zambia should prioritise to reduce the burden of its external debt on long-run economic development.', 'Zambia became the first African country to default on its sovereign debt during the COVID-19 pandemic, suspending a $42.5 million Eurobond coupon payment in November 2020. By 2023, Zambia''s external debt stood at approximately 120% of GDP, with debt-service obligations consuming nearly 30% of government revenue annually, severely crowding out public investment in infrastructure and education. A significant share of the debt is owed to bilateral creditors, including China, alongside multilateral institutions such as the IMF and World Bank.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T20:00:46.093+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('70fe2bd2-66a0-4c25-8823-f54e15de1477', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'HL', 'IB_ECON_201', 'P3', 'P3_part_b', 'recommend', 10, 'AO3', NULL, 'Recommend whether the government of Nigeria should prioritise granting subsidised licences to social enterprises over conventional private firms as its primary strategy for achieving economic diversification away from oil revenues.', 'Nigeria''s economy remains heavily dependent on crude oil, which accounted for approximately 87% of export earnings and 40% of government revenue in 2023, leaving it highly vulnerable to global commodity price shocks. The Nigerian government is currently evaluating two diversification pathways: subsidising social enterprises operating in agriculture, renewable energy, and digital services, or offering tax incentives to attract large-scale conventional private investment in manufacturing. A 2023 World Bank report estimates that social enterprises in sub-Saharan Africa reinvest an average of 65% of surpluses into local communities, compared with 18% for conventional firms of equivalent size.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T20:01:35.771+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('790672c9-ee8f-4eb5-8ea9-4d93374fb63b', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'HL', 'IB_ECON_203', 'P3', 'P3_part_b', 'recommend', 10, 'AO3', NULL, 'Recommend whether the Ethiopian government should prioritise expanding its state-owned industrial parks programme or redirecting fiscal resources toward direct cash transfers and rural agricultural subsidies as its primary interventionist development strategy.', 'Ethiopia''s manufacturing sector contributes only 6.4% of GDP, and youth unemployment stands at 27.3% (World Bank, 2023). The government is considering whether to expand its existing state-owned industrial parks programme — which currently hosts 22 parks offering subsidised utilities, land, and infrastructure to foreign and domestic firms — or to redirect fiscal resources toward direct cash transfers and rural agricultural subsidies to address poverty in the short run.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T20:02:04.567+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass'),
  ('2b2357e1-14c9-4c0b-bbde-1b7a3170ec02', 'IB_ECONOMICS', 'HL', 'IB_ECON_206', 'P3', 'P3_part_b', 'recommend', 10, 'AO3', NULL, 'Recommend whether the government of Zambia should accept a structural adjustment programme offered by the International Monetary Fund (IMF) as its primary strategy for addressing its current fiscal and debt crisis.', 'Zambia''s public debt reached approximately 143% of GDP in 2021, and the country defaulted on a $42.5 million Eurobond coupon payment in November 2020 — its first sovereign default in 25 years. Annual inflation rose to over 22% in early 2021, while foreign exchange reserves fell to below two months of import cover, prompting the government to open formal negotiations with the IMF for emergency balance-of-payments support.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'seed', 'claude_draft', 'f70bc413-64ca-44f4-a5e2-a970f60c53a5', '2026-05-22T20:02:35.845+00:00', 'gradd_original', 'V2', 'pass')
ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
